  <result aggregation-status="1" type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Annual Output Results</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator ascending="0" measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output Indicator</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">1.1	Percentage of households whose livelihood assets  have increased 12 months from project inception (e.g. livestock, agriculture production)
1.2	Number of savings and loans associations formed and active (number of women and men participating)
1.3	Number of value chain related  producer groups / Associations established / reactivated and % of women participating
1.4	%  increase of net annual income  achieved by producer groups and households attributable to project activities
2.1	Number of infrastructure rehabilitated/developed (by type)
2.2	Number of community members benefiting from  infrastructure rehabilitated/ developed by age and sex
2.3	Percentage of rehabilitated/ developed community assets linked with markets and value chains (by type of value chain)
2.4	Number of men and women employed in temporary labour intensive schemes
2.5	Percentage of people in target areas with improved perceptions of social cohesion within twelve to eighteen months of project, disaggregated by sex and age
3.1	Number of CBRMs established that are functional
3.2	% of community members who reported decrease in natural resource related conflicts.
3.3	% community members reporting increased access to dispute resolution mechanisms
3.4	% of natural resource conflicts successfully mediated
4.1 % of recruitment of Project Management Team
4.2 Number of monitoring field visits conducted
4.3 Number of STCCs and Board meetings held</narrative>
    </description>
    <baseline year="2016">
     <comment>
      <narrative xml:lang="EN">1.1	TBD
1.2	9 savings and loans associations in place
1.3	4 value chain related producer groups / Associations established/reactivated (with at least 53% women participating).
1.4	Average increase of 51.7% in annual incomes across all 4 value chains from $500 to about $758 in 2014/15
2.1	21 different infrastructure rehabilitated/developed (30% natural resource /70% socio-economic
2.2	1,000 community members benefiting from existing infrastructure
2.3	2.3	40% of rehabilitated/ developed community assets linked with markets and value chains 
2.4	463 labor (52% men and 48 % women) employed in temporary labour intensive schemes
2.5	50% of people in target areas with improved perceptions of social cohesion within twelve to eighteen months of project, 20% F
3.1	27 CBRMs currently in place and functional
3.2	60% of community members stating decrease in community conflicts as a result of project in CD and SD in 2015
3.3	TBD
3.4	TBD 
4.1 Programme Manager, RR Officer (NOA), 2 Programme Coordinators, Project Associate are in place
4.2 Each staff conducts average 3 monitoring field visits within a year
4.3 Average 3 STCCs and 1 board meeting held per year</narrative>
     </comment>
    </baseline>
